{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5oMwUANH6srUffZ5mF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `sqlmigrate` so it only wraps its output in BEGIN/COMMIT when the migration is atomic and the database can roll back DDL. I haven't run any tests, and I didn't add one.\n\nThe change is one line in `django/core/management/commands/sqlmigrate.py`:\n\n```python\nself.output_transaction = migration.atomic and connection.features.can_rollback_ddl\n```\n\nThis matches the condition the migration executor uses for the outer transaction. The issue suggests a test in `tests/migrations/test_commands.py` that mocks `connection.features.can_rollback_ddl` to False. I left that out because the rules say not to edit test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":19079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":939},"output_tokens":219,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01f76b69-9e07-45cb-a582-79588cd82873","uuid":"83655ac3-b62d-4551-aee6-09891d154990","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:37:59.986Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5oMp2J9zvh73WRnwz1"}
